---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy" description="Privacy policy of Planexus GmbH — information on the handling of your personal data pursuant to the GDPR (DSGVO)." canonical="/en/privacy">
  <div class="pt-20 min-h-screen bg-white">
    <section class="py-20 bg-slate-50 border-b border-gray-100">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 text-center">Privacy policy</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-lg prose-slate">

          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-8 text-sm leading-relaxed bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-gray-100">
            This English translation of the privacy policy is provided for convenience. The <a href="/datenschutz" class="font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">German version</a> is legally authoritative. The following information explains how we process personal data under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR / DSGVO) and applicable German data-protection law.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">1. Data protection at a glance</h2>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">General information</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            The following notes provide a simple overview of what happens to your personal data when you visit this website. Personal data is any data with which you can be personally identified. Detailed information on data protection can be found in the privacy policy set out below.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Data collection on this website</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
            <strong>Who is responsible for data collection on this website?</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            Data processing on this website is carried out by the website operator. You can find the operator’s contact details in the section “Information on the controller” in this privacy policy.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">2. Controller</h2>

          <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl mb-8">
            <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Planexus GmbH</p>
            <p class="text-gray-600">
              Am Steinbach 8<br />
              72459 Albstadt<br />
              Germany
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-600 mt-4">
              Telephone: <a href="tel:+4974357519700" class="text-primary hover:underline">+49 7435 7519 700</a><br />
              Email: <a href="mailto:info@planexus.de" class="text-primary hover:underline">info@planexus.de</a>
            </p>
          </div>

          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            The controller is the natural or legal person who, alone or jointly with others, determines the purposes and means of the processing of personal data (e.g. names, email addresses or similar).
          </p>

          <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">3. Your rights</h2>

          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">You have the right at any time to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Obtain information about the data we store about you (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Request rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Request erasure of your data (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Request restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Request data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR)</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">4. Data collection on this website</h2>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Server log files</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
            The provider of the pages automatically collects and stores information in so-called server log files, which your browser automatically transmits to us. These are:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 mb-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Browser type and browser version</li>
            <li>Operating system used</li>
            <li>Referrer URL</li>
            <li>Host name of the accessing computer</li>
            <li>Time of the server request</li>
            <li>IP address</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            This data is not combined with other data sources. Collection is based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The website operator has a legitimate interest in the technically error-free presentation and optimisation of the website — for this, the server log files must be collected.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Contact form</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            If you send us enquiries via the contact form, your details from the enquiry form, including the contact data you provide there, will be stored by us for the purpose of processing the enquiry and in case of follow-up questions. We do not pass on this data without your consent. Processing of this data is based on Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if your enquiry is related to the performance of a contract or is necessary for the implementation of pre-contractual measures.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Cookies and consent management</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
            On your first visit to our website you will be asked for your consent via a cookie banner. You can choose between “Accept all”, “Necessary only” and individual settings. Your selection is stored locally in your browser and can be changed at any time via the “Cookie settings” link in the footer.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            We distinguish the following categories: <strong>Necessary cookies</strong> (required for operation of the website), <strong>Statistics</strong> (e.g. Google Analytics) and <strong>Marketing</strong> (e.g. Google Ads). Statistics and marketing cookies are set only after your express consent. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Google Tag Manager &amp; Consent Mode</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
            This website uses Google Tag Manager (GTM), a tag-management service of Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. We manage website tags centrally via GTM — including Google Analytics 4 and Google Ads.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
            We use <strong>Google Consent Mode V2</strong>. Tracking services are blocked by default and activated only after your consent. Consent signals are transmitted to Google via the <code class="text-sm bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">dataLayer</code>. The following consent types are recorded: <code class="text-sm bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">analytics_storage</code> (statistics), <code class="text-sm bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">ad_storage</code>, <code class="text-sm bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">ad_user_data</code> and <code class="text-sm bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">ad_personalization</code> (marketing/Google Ads).
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
            If you have allowed statistics cookies, information about your use of this website (e.g. pages visited, dwell time, source of access) is transmitted to Google. If you have allowed marketing cookies, conversion data and remarketing information for Google Ads may be processed.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
            The provider is Google Ireland Limited. Where data is transferred to the USA, Google relies on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses. Further information: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-primary hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            You can additionally prevent collection by Google Analytics by installing the browser add-on: <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="text-primary hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>
          </p>

          <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">5. SSL / TLS encryption</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            For security reasons and to protect the transmission of confidential content, such as orders or enquiries that you send to us as site operator, this site uses SSL or TLS encryption. You can recognise an encrypted connection by the fact that the browser address bar changes from “http://” to “https://” and by the padlock symbol in your browser bar. When SSL or TLS encryption is activated, the data you transmit to us cannot be read by third parties.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">6. Retention period</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            Unless a more specific retention period is stated in this privacy policy, your personal data remains with us until the purpose for data processing ceases to apply. If you assert a legitimate request for erasure or withdraw consent to data processing, your data will be deleted unless we have other legally permissible reasons for storing your personal data (e.g. tax or commercial-law retention periods); in the latter case, erasure takes place after those reasons cease to apply.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">7. Currency and amendment of this privacy policy</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            This privacy policy is currently valid and dated July 2026. As a result of the further development of our website and offerings, or due to changed statutory or official requirements, it may become necessary to amend this privacy policy.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 mt-12">
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Do you have questions about data protection? <a href="/en/contact" class="font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">Contact us</a> directly. Further information about our company is available in the <a href="/en/imprint" class="font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">imprint</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
